MEMMGR block-table realloc/compaction (3439/345c/3584/385c/3894): byte-scale the parallel
block-info tables (Ghidra double-scaled `&DAT + i*4` -> i*16, so the compaction copied/reindexed
the wrong blocks and the KDV chunk buffer's 8-byte header -- the 'xVDK'/'pVDK'/'iVDK' MAGIC -- was
not preserved across a resize, so 6f3e's magic dispatch never matched and the RLE decoder ran with
width=height=0 -> read off the buffer end -> SIGSEGV).

The extender MEMMGR keeps parallel per-block arrays indexed by block number (stride 4 bytes):
  0x28ac = block key/handle ; 0x2a3c = block base ptr ; 0x2bcc = block size ; 0x2bd0 ...
  0x2d5c/0x2d60 = alignment/aux ; 0x2eec = flags.  The asm indexes them `[reg*4 + 0xXXXX]` (a BYTE
offset of reg*4).  Ghidra typed the base symbols as 4-byte scalars, so `&DAT_0000_2a3c + iVar6 * 4`
is pointer arithmetic that scales by the element size again (byte +iVar6*16) -> wrong slot.  The
`(&DAT_0000_28ac)[i]` indexed forms are already the correct stride-4 and are left as-is; only the
explicit `&DAT + expr * 4` forms (2a3c / 2bd0 / 2d5c / 2d60) are wrong.  Restore each to a byte
offset off the table base -- `(char *)&DAT_0000_XXXX + expr * 4` -- matching the asm.  (The 3661
copy of this class is fixed in patch 078; the `(int)&DAT_0000_28a5 + ... + 3` head-block form is
integer byte arithmetic and stays.)  asm-verified (e.g. 345c 0x350c..0x3523: mov/mov DWORD PTR
[ebx*4+0x28ac]/[ebx*4+0x2bcc]/[ebx*4+0x2a3c]).
